Subject: Cost-Effective Shipping Plan Across Source-Destination Network
Date: [DATE]

Situation
We operate a network of source locations (warehouses, factories, and distribution centers) and a network of destination points (stores, customers, and regional hubs). Each source has limited inventory, and each destination has a defined need to be fulfilled. All shipments must be in whole-unit quantities, with no partial loads allowed. The objective is to move goods at the lowest total transport cost while ensuring every destination obtains its required quantity and no source is drawn beyond its available stock. Achieving this supports meaningful cost savings and higher levels of customer satisfaction.

Problem
The challenge is to determine a practical shipment plan that uses the available routes, which have varying costs, to meet all destination demands without exceeding any source’s inventory. The plan should reflect the lowest possible total shipping cost across the network while respecting the whole-unit shipment rule.

